# Emergency banner

The publishing emergency banner places urgent information above ordinary content. Its government-specific event categories do not transfer to a household dashboard. [Official publishing guidance](https://design-guide.publishing.service.gov.uk/components/emergency-banner/).

**Reference pattern.** The examples document a local adaptation; they do not add a publishing backend or a new Home Assistant capability.

## When to use it

Reserve an equivalent household alert for a verified, current condition that needs immediate attention. Include what happened, where, when it was reported and the relevant next action. Keep routine maintenance, expiry reminders and disconnected non-critical sensors in ordinary status components.

## Structure and behaviour

Name the condition in text and retain the underlying integration timestamp and availability. A new urgent alert can be announced once; an already present alert should remain readable without repeatedly interrupting assistive technology. Do not use colour alone to distinguish severity.

## Home Assistant boundary

The theme does not decide that a condition is an emergency, act as an alarm system or replace independent warning equipment. These examples are static design specimens labelled as examples. No simulated emergency is injected into HA, and no government emergency branding is reused.

